## 2. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp` — `GgufModel::find()` stores dangling `const TensorInfo*` into `shards_[i]->tensors()`

**Responsibilities.** `GgufModel` builds `index_` mapping name → `(shard_index, const TensorInfo*)`. The pointer points into the `std::vector<TensorInfo>` owned by each `GgufFile`. If a `GgufFile` were ever moved or its vector reallocated, the pointer would dangle. Currently `GgufFile` is non-copyable and the vectors are built once in `parse()`, so this is safe today, but the invariant is undocumented and fragile.

**Proposed change.** Store the tensor index within the shard's vector instead of a raw pointer, and resolve through `shards_[i]->tensors()[idx]`.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@ public:
     explicit GgufModel(const std::vector<std::string>& paths) {
         if (paths.empty()) throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: a model needs at least one shard");
         for (const auto& p : paths) shards_.push_back(std::make_unique<GgufFile>(p));
         validate_split();
         for (size_t i = 0; i < shards_.size(); ++i)
-            for (const auto& t : shards_[i]->tensors()) {
-                const auto ins = index_.emplace(t.name, std::make_pair(i, &t));
+            for (size_t j = 0; j < shards_[i]->tensors().size(); ++j) {
+                const auto& t = shards_[i]->tensors()[j];
+                const auto ins = index_.emplace(t.name, std::make_pair(i, j));
                 if (!ins.second)
                     throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: tensor " + t.name + " is in two shards (" +
                                              shards_[ins.first->second.first]->path() + " and " +
                                              shards_[i]->path() + ")");
             }
     }
@@ -325,9 +325,9 @@ public:
     /// The tensor named `name` (its shard index in `*shard`), or nullptr.
     const TensorInfo* find(const std::string& name, size_t* shard = nullptr) const {
         const auto it = index_.find(name);
         if (it == index_.end()) return nullptr;
-        if (shard) *shard = it->second.first;
-        return it->second.second;
+        if (shard) *shard = it->second.first;
+        return &shards_[it->second.first]->tensors()[it->second.second];
     }
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@ private:
     std::vector<std::unique_ptr<GgufFile>> shards_;
-    std::map<std::string, std::pair<size_t, const TensorInfo*>> index_;
+    std::map<std::string, std::pair<size_t, size_t>> index_;
 };
```

**Verification cases.**
1. `gguf_split_test` constructs a `GgufModel` from synthetic shards, calls `find()` for every tensor name, and verifies the returned pointer's `name` and `type` match the expected tensor.
2. A new unit test constructs a `GgufModel`, calls `find()` for a name, then destroys and re-creates the model from the same paths; confirm no ASAN/valgrind error and identical results.

